Rule 1 (tensor–tensor inputs must be broadcastable when ranks match)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : (shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)) ∨ (shape(v_1, i) = 1) ∨ (shape(v_2, i) = 1)
>>
Rule 4 (with tensor other and same rank, out must match the broadcasted shape)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ndim(v_3) = ndim(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_3) = 0 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : ((shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∧ shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_1, i)) ∨ (shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∧ shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_2, i)) ∨ (shape(v_2, i) = 1 ∧ shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_1, i)))
>>
Rule 5 (complex tensor inputs must be compared with complex tensors)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if 9 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10 then 9 ≤ dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 10
>>
Rule 6 (bool input compared with a scalar number must use 0 or 1)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : float} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 0 then (v_2 = 0 ∨ v_2 = 1)
